Hi,

On an ASUS ROG STRIX X870E-E GAMING WIFI7 NEO (Ryzen 9 9950X3D2), the=20
USB 3 half of an onboard ASMedia ASM2074 hub never enumerates. Its USB 2=20
half (174c:2174) and the devices behind it work, so that port group is=20
stuck at 480M. Windows 11 on the same machine enumerates both halves on=20
the same root port.

Host: AMD Promontory 21 xHCI at 0000:0f:00.0, hcc params 0x0200ef81, hci=20
version 0x110. DMI/BIOS, lspci and lsusb -v are in asm2074-info.txt.

Every boot:

[ 5.478608] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 9.648279] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 9.851716] usb 9-5: device not accepting address 3, error -71

[ 14.138394] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 18.307806] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 18.515615] usb 9-5: device not accepting address 4, error -71

[ 23.278983] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 27.448442] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 27.659615] usb 9-5: device not accepting address 6, error -71

[ 31.938623] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 36.107891] usb 9-5: Device not responding to setup address.

[ 36.315597] usb 9-5: device not accepting address 7, error -71

[ 36.328157] usb usb9-port5: unable to enumerate USB device

Topology (bus 8 =3D USB 2 roothub, bus 9 =3D USB 3 roothub of 0f:00.0):

/: Bus 008.Port 001: Dev 001, Class=3Droot_hub,=20
Driver=3Dxhci-pci-prom21/12p, 480M |__ Port 004: Dev 003, Class=3DHub,=20
Driver=3Dhub/4p, 480M ASM1174 174c:2274 |__ Port 005: Dev 004, Class=3DHub,=
=20
Driver=3Dhub/4p, 480M ASM2074 174c:2174

/: Bus 009.Port 001: Dev 001, Class=3Droot_hub, Driver=3Dxhci-pci-prom21/5p=
,=20
20000M/x2 |__ Port 004: Dev 002, Class=3DHub, Driver=3Dhub/4p, 5000M ASM117=
4=20
174c:3274 (port 5 =3D ASM2074 SuperSpeed half, 174c:3174 - never enumerates=
)

The ASM1174 on the neighbouring port pair works fine at 5000M.

Windows 11 on the same hardware lists all four hub functions as OK,=20
including USB\VID_174C&PID_3174\8&15CD6C09&0&5 on root port 5.

- Same failure on 7.2.9-2-cachyos and 6.18.55-2-cachyos-lts (bus is=20
numbered 4 on 6.18: usb 4-5 / usb4-port5).

- Also reproduces at runtime after unbind/bind of 0000:0f:00.0.

- Side effect: while the ~31 s of retries run, other devices on that=20
controller enumerate late and initramfs switch-root waits until ~40 s.

Attached (xz): dmesg with dyndbg "module usbcore +p; module xhci_hcd +p"=20
and the xhci-hcd trace events, both covering an unbind/bind of=20
0000:0f:00.0 on 7.2.9.

These are CachyOS kernels; happy to test mainline or patches.

Thanks,

Brian Tucker

